"You" means the person or organization exercising rights under this license.

2. What you may do, free of charge

Subject to this license, the Licensor grants you a worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
non-sublicensable, royalty-free license to:

  a) read, study, audit and review the Software;
  b) run, test and modify the Software privately, on local development chains and public test
     networks, to learn how it works, to check its security, or to evaluate whether to work with
     the Licensor;
  c) report security vulnerabilities to the Licensor (see SECURITY.md) and discuss the Software
     publicly, quoting short excerpts with attribution;
  d) contribute to the Software: fork it on GitHub and propose changes to the Licensor's
     repository (issues, pull requests). Forks may be used only to prepare such contributions;
  e) when the Licensor has entered the Software into a Competition or applied for a grant or
     investment with it: read, run and test it as a judge, organizer, reviewer or investor, to
     assess that entry or application.

These free uses are for learning, checking and helping only. They do not include any use with
Real Value, any Competition, any product or service, or publishing the Software or a Derivative
anywhere except as a fork for contributions.

3. What requires written permission from the Licensor

  a) Competitions: only the Licensor, or a team that the Licensor joins or authorizes with written
